  </header>
  <!-- 01 · COMPARE -->
  <section class="g-dark" id="bar">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="op-n" data-v9-reveal=""><b>{values[top]}%</b><span>{sector.copy.opening}</span></div>
      <h2 data-v9-reveal="" style="--d:60ms">Same six skills. A different shape.</h2>
      <p class="lead" data-v9-reveal="" style="--d:120ms">{sector.copy.compareLead}</p>
      <div class="ix-lab" data-me={sector.slug} data-v9-reveal="" style="--d:160ms">
        <div class="ix-panel">
          <div class="ix-panel-top">
            <span class="ix-key"><i class="a"></i>{sector.name}</span><span class="ix-key"
              ><i class="b"></i><span id="ixBName">{comparison.name}</span></span
            >
          </div>
          <p class="ix-read" id="ixRead">{comparisonRead}</p>
          <ul class="ix-cbars" id="ixC">
            {
              skills.map((skill, i) => (
                <li data-d={i} class:list={{ hot: i === difference }}>
                  <>
                    <span class="ix-dn">{skill}</span>
                    <span class="ix-pair">
                      <>
                        <span class="ix-tr ix-tr--a">
                          <i style={`--v:${values[i]}`} />
                        </span>
                        <span class="ix-tr ix-tr--b">
                          <i style={`--v:${otherValues[i]}`} />
                        </span>
                      </>
                    </span>
                    <b>
                      <>
                        <span class="ix-a">{values[i]}</span>
                        <span class="ix-b">{otherValues[i]}</span>
                      </>
                    </b>
                  </>
                </li>
              ))
            }
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="ix-cmps-w">
          <span class="ql">Compare with</span><div aria-label="Compare with" class="ix-cmps" role="tablist">
            {
              sectors
                .filter((s) => s.slug !== sector.slug)
                .map((s) => (
                  <button
                    hidden
                    class="ix-cmp"
                    type="button"
                    role="tab"
                    aria-selected={s.slug === comparison.slug ? 'true' : 'false'}
                    data-s={s.slug}
                  >
                    {s.name}
                  </button>
                ))
            }
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <!-- 02 · MISSES -->
  <section class="g-white" id="misses">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow" data-v9-reveal=""><span class="tick">\</span> 02 · Where a generic screen breaks</div>
      <h2 data-v9-reveal="" style="--d:60ms">{sector.copy.missesHeading}</h2>
      <p class="lead" data-v9-reveal="" style="--d:120ms">
        None of them are exotic. They’re invisible to anyone assessing from outside the sector, which is most of the
        people doing the assessing.
      </p>
      <ol class="ix-miss">
        {
          sector.misses.map((miss, i) => (
            <li data-v9-reveal style={`--d:${i * 70}ms`}>
              <>
                <span class="ab-k">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
                <div>
                  <>
                    <h3>{miss.title}</h3>
                    <span class="ix-lbl">{miss.label}</span>
                  </>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <>
                    <p>{miss.body}</p>
                    <p class="ix-tell">
                      <span>Where it shows up</span>
                      {miss.tell.replace(/^Where it shows up: /, '')}
                    </p>
                  </>
                </div>
              </>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>
  <!-- 03 · QUESTIONS -->
  <section class="g-paper" id="ask">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow" data-v9-reveal=""><span class="tick">\</span> 03 · What we actually ask</div>
      <h2 data-v9-reveal="" style="--d:60ms">Three questions. Three thin answers.</h2>
      <p class="lead" data-v9-reveal="" style="--d:120ms">
        Every question comes off the candidate’s own CV, so these show the shape. The right-hand column is the part a
        generic interviewer can’t supply.
      </p>
      <div class="ix-qs">
        {
          sector.questions.map((question, i) => (
            <article class="ix-q" data-v9-reveal style={`--d:${i * 80}ms`}>
              <>
                <span class="ab-k">Q{i + 1}</span>
                <h3>{question.q}</h3>
                <div class="ix-q-g">
                  <>
                    <div>
                      <>
                        <span class="ix-lbl">A thin answer</span>
                        <p class="ix-thin">
                          <span>{question.thin}</span>
                        </p>
                      </>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                      <>
                        <span class="ix-lbl">What the expert listens for</span>
                        <p>{question.listeningFor}</p>
                      </>
                    </div>
                  </>
                </div>
              </>
            </article>
          ))
        }
      </div>
      <p class="decide" data-v9-reveal="">
        <b>A correct answer with no reasoning behind it proves nothing.</b> That line is written into how we score, and this
        sector is where it earns its keep.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <!-- 04 · ROLES + BENCH -->
  <section class="g-dark" id="roles">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow" data-v9-reveal=""><span class="tick">\</span> 04 · Roles and interviewers</div>
      <h2 data-v9-reveal="" style="--d:60ms">Every level, one guarantee.</h2>
      <p class="lead" data-v9-reveal="" style="--d:120ms">{sector.copy.rolesLead}</p>
      <div class="ix-rb">
        <ul class="ix-roles">
          {
            sector.roles.map((role, i) => (
              <li data-v9-reveal style={`--d:${i * 40}ms`}>
                <>
                  <b>{role.family}</b>
                  <span>{role.levels}</span>
                </>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
        <div class="ix-bench" data-v9-reveal="" style="--d:120ms">
          <span class="ql">{sector.copy.benchHeading}</span>
          <ul>{sector.bench.map((person) => <li>{person}</li>)}</ul>
          <span class="ql">What that changes</span>
          <ul class="ix-chg">
            <li>The follow-up lands, because they know where answers usually thin out.</li><li>
              Titles get read against what the person was accountable for.
            </li><li>A weak answer gets a second chance before it gets a low score.</li><li>
              The write-up is in the language your hiring manager already uses.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="ix-miss-r" data-v9-reveal="">
        Not seeing your role? <a class="link" href={contact}>Tell us what you’re hiring for ›</a> We’ll say straight away
        whether it’s our ground.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <!-- 05 · FAQ -->
  <section class="faq g-paper">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="faq-top">
        <div class="faq-aside">
          <div class="eyebrow" data-v9-reveal=""><span class="tick">\</span> 05 · Before you brief us</div>
          <h2 data-v9-reveal="" style="--d:60ms">What teams ask first.</h2>
          <div class="faq-ask" data-v9-reveal="" style="--d:180ms">
            <p class="faq-ask-q">Didn’t see yours?</p>
            <a href={contact}>Ask us anything <span aria-hidden="true" class="ar">→</span></a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-list" data-v9-reveal="" style="--d:120ms">
          {
            sector.faq.map((faq, i) => (
              <details class="faq-item" open={i === 0}>
                <>
                  <summary class="faq-q">
                    <>
                      <span>{faq.q}</span>
                      <span class="faq-ic" aria-hidden="true" />
                    </>
                  </summary>
                  <div class="faq-a">
                    <div>
                      <p>{faq.a}</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </>
              </details>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <!-- CLOSE -->
  <section class="start g-white" id="start">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="start-head">
        <div class="eyebrow" data-v9-reveal="" style="justify-content:center">
          <span class="tick">\</span> Start here
        </div>
        <h2 data-v9-reveal="" style="--d:60ms">
          Tell us the role. Three names in <span class="hd-word"
            >36 hours.<svg
              aria-hidden="true"
              class="hd-underline hd-ink"
              preserveAspectRatio="none"
              viewBox="0 0 120 12"
              ><path d="M3,8 Q34,3.5 62,6.5 Q92,9 117,5 Q92,11.2 62,9.2 Q34,6.4 3,8.7 Z"></path></svg
            ></span
          >
        </h2>
      </div>
      <p class="lead" data-v9-reveal="" style="--d:120ms">{sector.copy.closingLead}</p>
      <div class="cta-row" data-v9-reveal="" style="--d:180ms">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={contact}>Brief a role</a>
        <a class="link" href={v9Href('/__v9/industries', Astro.url.pathname)}>Other sectors ›</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="g-white fn-sec" id="sources">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="fn-end">
        <p class="ql">Sources</p><ol class="fn-list">
          <li id="src-1">
            <span class="fn-t"
              ><a href={sector.market.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{sector.market.source}</a></span
            >
          </li>
        </ol><a class="link" href={v9Href('/__v9/about', Astro.url.pathname)}>How we work with numbers ›</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
<script>
  import '../../../scripts/v9/editorial';
</script>
